    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d180">

                <pb facs="0489" n="403" sameAs="frus:frus1873p1v1/pg403"/>

                <head>No. 178.<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"><persName corresp="#p_SET1" type="from"
                            >Sir Edward Thornton</persName> to Mr. <persName corresp="#p_HF1"
                            type="to">Fish</persName>.</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1873-01-24"><hi rendition="#italic">January</hi> 24, 1873</date>.
                        (Received January 25.)</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: With reference to my note of the 4th
                    ultimo, inclosing, as another legislative document connected with the Treaty of
                    Washington, of May 8, 1871, a certified copy of an act of the legislature of
                    Canada, I have now the honor to forward herewith, in connection with that
                    treaty, for <pb facs="0490" n="404" xml:id="pg404"/> your information, a copy of
                    the act passed on the 6th of August last by the Parliament of the United Kingdom
                    to carry into effect the said treaty between Her Majesty and the United States
                    of America, as regards the British Colonies in North America.</p>
                <p>I have, &amp;c.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed><persName corresp="#p_SET1">EDW’D. THORNTON</persName>.</signed>
                </closer>



                <xi:include href="d180-a1.xml" xpointer="d180-a1"/>
